From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kadaxo <105596590+kadaxo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:41:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Give buffers new storage when their whole contents are
 replaced

EditBufferData overwrote the buffer with glBufferSubData. When the GPU
may still be reading that buffer, macOS's OpenGL (which runs on Metal)
flushes and waits for the GPU, and constant buffers are edited for nearly
every draw: on a MacBook Pro the app spent 82% of its main thread there
and ran at about 12 frames per second. Replacing the whole buffer with
glBufferData lets the driver use fresh storage without waiting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/yds_opengl_device.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/yds_opengl_device.cpp b/src/yds_opengl_device.cpp
index 992f967e..d76465b7 100644
--- a/src/yds_opengl_device.cpp
+++ b/src/yds_opengl_device.cpp
@@ -650,8 +650,12 @@ ysError ysOpenGLDevice::EditBufferData(ysGPUBuffer *buffer, char *data) {
     ysOpenGLGPUBuffer *openglBuffer = static_cast<ysOpenGLGPUBuffer *>(buffer);
     int target = openglBuffer->GetTarget();
 
+    // The whole buffer is replaced, so give it new storage instead of
+    // overwriting the old one: glBufferSubData on a buffer the GPU may still
+    // be reading makes some drivers (macOS's OpenGL on Metal) flush and wait
+    // for the GPU, and constant buffers are edited for nearly every draw
     m_realContext->glBindBuffer(target, openglBuffer->m_bufferHandle);
-    m_realContext->glBufferSubData(target, 0, openglBuffer->GetSize(), data);
+    m_realContext->glBufferData(target, openglBuffer->GetSize(), data, GL_DYNAMIC_DRAW);
 
     // Restore Previous State
     if (previous != buffer) {
